Proposed accompanying tests (tests/Feature/Integrations/N8nReminderOutboxFeedPassTest.php):
  1. enabled + pending event  -> one feed poll delivers it (Http::fake 200), event becomes delivered.
  2. a second poll within the minute does not call the dispatcher again (Cache::add guard).
  3. disabled integration     -> no HTTP call, feed response unchanged.
  4. dispatcher throws        -> feed still returns 200 with its normal JSON (error logged).
  5. non-CI user poll         -> outbox pass still runs; feed still returns the empty payload.
  6. a pending cancellation supersedes an older pending reschedule of the same subject -> only the
     cancellation is sent (existing dispatcher behaviour, exercised through the feed).

Configuration (no code): N8N_REMINDERS_MAX_ATTEMPTS=30 in production. With the existing 360-minute
backoff cap this keeps retrying for about 5.3 days (511 min + 20 x 360 min) instead of about
8.5 hours (1+2+...+256 = 511 min with the default 10) before an event becomes
'failed', because 'failed' can only be re-queued via the CLI, which InfinityFree lacks.
